/commander
/dist/
*.test
.DS_Store

# The delegate CLI, built with `go build -o ~/.local/bin/delegate ./cmd/delegate`.
# A build into the repo root was committed once (4511c93, 9.6 MB) — the same
# mistake the psmux note below exists to prevent, and worse: a Go binary embeds
# the absolute source paths it was built from, so that one carried the author's
# home directory, and export-public.sh ships tracked files verbatim via
# `git archive HEAD`. The companion grep tripwire does not catch it (BSD grep
# skips the over-long lines a binary is made of), so nothing would have stopped
# it reaching the public mirror.
/delegate

# Wails GUI build output
/build/bin/
frontend/dist/
frontend/node_modules/
/.playwright-mcp/
build/darwin/Info.dev.plist
frontend/test-results/
frontend/playwright-report/
frontend/package.json.md5

# Bundled psmux, fetched and hash-verified by build.ps1 (Ensure-PsmuxAsset).
# Deliberately not committed: a 7 MB binary would sit in every clone's history
# forever, and the pin in build.ps1 gives the same reproducibility for free.
internal/deps/assets/

# agent scratch (progress ledgers, task briefs, review diffs)
/.superpowers/
